## Setting 1 Deep Dive — The Geometric Face

[![Marquise Diamond Signet Ring in 14K Yellow Gold, single stone geometric face](/images/blue-nile-marquise-diamond-signet-ring-mens-yellow-gold.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/marquise-diamond-signet-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-1-5-ct-tw-item-146160?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=Image)

The geometric face setting puts one cut stone at the center. No accent diamonds. No pavé border. The stone sits in a bezel or open prong mount. The face IS the girdle-to-table of that stone.

**Why this matters for men:** A single-stone signet looks architectural. The marquise shape gives the face a pointed-oval footprint that reads differently from every angle. The emerald cut gives a rectangular face that reads modern and deliberate.

Both shapes appear across men's fine jewelry. See [men's emerald cut ring](https://www.diamondcritics.com/mens-emerald-cut-ring) for how the shape translates across other ring styles.

**The Marquise Signet — $2,100**

The [Marquise Diamond Signet Ring in 14k yellow gold](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/marquise-diamond-signet-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-1-5-ct-tw-item-146160?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) carries a 1/5 ct. tw. stone in a heavy mount. 1/5 ct isn't large in isolation. But the elongated shape covers more face area than a round of equal weight — so it reads bigger.

Yellow gold is the correct metal for marquise on a signet. The warmth of 14K yellow gold and the warmth of a marquise cut reinforce each other. White gold creates a colder contrast that works differently — better for the emerald cut.

**The Emerald Diamond Signet — ~~$1,470**

The [Emerald Diamond Signet Ring in 14k white gold](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/emerald-diamond-signet-ring-in-14k-white-gold-1-5-ct-tw-item-146161?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) uses 1/5 ct. tw. Emerald cut, stepped facets, rectangular face. White gold, cool tone, modern line. This is the most architecturally modern signet here.

It pairs well with a [men's diamond eternity band](https://www.diamondcritics.com/mens-diamond-eternity-band) on the other hand — both are geometric and structured. Currently 30% off at approximately $1,029. That makes it the best-priced geometric face ring on this list.

**The Classic 5/8-Carat — $2,400**

The [Diamond Signet Ring in 14k yellow gold, 5/8 ct. tw.](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/diamond-signet-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-5-8-ct-tw-item-147874?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the highest-carat option here. 5/8 ct. tw. spread across the full face — the classic signet silhouette. Heavy gold shank, wide face, serious diamond presence.

This is the ring you feel on your finger. It has weight. Men who want that physical presence on their hand should start here.

| Setting | Stone | Metal | Price | What this means |
|---------|-------|-------|-------|-----------------|
| Marquise Signet | 1/5 ct. tw. | 14K Yellow | $2,100 | Pointed face, most distinctive silhouette |
| Emerald Signet | 1/5 ct. tw. | 14K White | ~~$1,470~~ | Rectangular, modern, 30% off now |
| Classic 5/8ct Signet | 5/8 ct. tw. | 14K Yellow | $2,400 | Largest stone weight, most substantial feel |

