## Setting 2 Deep Dive — The Pavé Cluster

[![Diamond Star Signet Ring in 14K Yellow Gold, pavé cluster entry option](/images/blue-nile-diamond-star-signet-ring-yellow-gold.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/diamond-star-signet-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-257139?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=Image)

Pavé cluster signets are the opposite philosophy from the geometric face. Instead of one large stone, you get many small stones spread across the face in a deliberate pattern. Each stone contributes to a larger image — a star, a heart, an oval.

The entry point here is significantly lower: $756 on sale versus $2,100 for a marquise. That gap doesn't reflect quality — it reflects caratage. Smaller stones cost less per piece.

The result still reads as a diamond ring from across the room.

**Diamond Star Signet — From ~~$756**

The [Diamond Star Signet Ring in 14k yellow gold](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/diamond-star-signet-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-257139?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the entry point for men's pavé signets. Currently 30% off from $756. The star pattern — five-point diamond arrangement centered on yellow gold — is simple, clean, and wears every day.

This pairs well with a [men's diamond wedding band](https://www.diamondcritics.com/mens-diamond-wedding-band) if you want both hands stacked. Different metals, same diamond presence.

Same design available in [rose gold, also ~~$756](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/diamond-star-signet-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-item-257140?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and [white gold, originally $1,080](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/diamond-star-signet-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-257138?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). The white gold version costs more because the alloy content differs — not because the diamonds are better.

**Heart Bezel Signets — Lab vs Natural**

This is where the lab-vs-natural price difference shows most clearly on a signet.

The [Heart Lab-Grown Diamond Bezel Signet in yellow gold](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/heart-lab-grown-diamond-bezel-signet-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-311310?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is currently ~~$1,120. The natural version — the [Heart Diamond Bezel Signet Ring, same yellow gold](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/heart-diamond-bezel-signet-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-146162?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — is $2,100. Same metal, same design, same face shape.

The gap is entirely the diamond origin. For the lab trade-off in men's rings, the [men's lab grown diamond ring](https://www.diamondcritics.com/mens-lab-grown-diamond-ring) guide applies directly to signets.

**Pavé Heart Lab Signet by James Allen — ~~$1,475**

The [Pavé Heart Signet by James Allen](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/pave-heart-signet-ring-with-075-ctw-round-lab-grown-diamonds-in-14k-yellow-gold-by-james-allen-item-316371?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) gives you more carat weight than the star. 0.75 CTW lab covers the full heart face. It reads visually heavy for ~~$1,475 — the best face coverage under $1,500 here.

**Modern Pavé Oval — $5,200**

[![Modern Pavé Oval Signet Ring in 14K Yellow Gold, full face diamond coverage](/images/blue-nile-pave-oval-diamond-signet-ring-mens-yellow-gold.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/modern-pave-oval-signet-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-with-diamonds-item-321943?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=Image)

The [Modern Pavé Oval Signet Ring in yellow gold](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/modern-pave-oval-signet-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-with-diamonds-item-321943?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the highest-priced ring here at $5,200. The oval face has full pavé coverage, edge to edge. The shank is substantial — this isn't a daily driver.

It's a statement ring or a collector's piece — the most evolved signet available. No other men's signet goes further.

Compare it to a [men's cushion cut ring](https://www.diamondcritics.com/mens-cushion-cut-ring) if you're weighing bold face designs across categories.

