## Setting 3 Deep Dive — The Initial Letter Collection

[![Diamond B Initial Signet Ring in 14K Yellow Gold By James Allen, diamond monogram face](/images/blue-nile-diamond-initial-signet-ring-yellow-gold.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/diamond-b-initial-signet-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-by-james-allen-item-304266?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=Image)

The initial letter collection is the most personal of the three settings. It is also the most heritage-specific. Diamond-set monogram on a gold face — your letter, chosen once, worn for decades or passed down.

James Allen (now a Blue Nile brand since August 2026) produces the entire A–Z collection in three metals. The price is flat: $1,405 regardless of letter, regardless of metal. No premium for rare letters.

No discount for common ones. This is unusual in fine jewelry — the value is in personalization, not production difficulty.

All 26 letters are available in:
- **14K Yellow Gold** — classic, warmest tone, works with most skin tones
- **14K White Gold** — coolest tone, modern, pairs with silver or platinum elsewhere on the hand
- **14K Rose Gold** — unique, warm-pink tone, increasingly worn by men who want color

The letter design traces the initial in small diamonds against the gold face. Up close, you read the letter. At distance, you see diamond coverage and a signet face.

**Who should pick the initial letter setting:** Any man giving this ring as a meaningful gift (father to son, partner to partner, milestone marker). Any man who wants something singular — not a catalog style but a personalized piece. Any man building a [men's diamond engagement ring](https://www.diamondcritics.com/mens-diamond-engagement-ring) with a matching band and wants the signet to anchor the story.

